  "question": {
    "text": "Solution of $2^x+2^{|x|} \\geq 2 \\sqrt{2}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QvFCe",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\infty, \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YLlkh",
      "text": "$(0, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uUdi5",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pB8Jf",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\infty, \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\right] \\cup\\left[\\frac{1}{2}, \\infty\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$2^x+2^{|x|} \\geq 2 \\sqrt{2}$ ...(i)<br />Case I: $x \\geq 0$, then Eq. (i) becomes<br />$2^x+2^x \\geq 2 \\sqrt{2}$<br />$\\Rightarrow 2^x \\geq \\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow x \\geq \\frac{1}{2}$<br />Case II: $x < 0$, then Eq. (i) becomes<br />$2^x+2^{-x} \\geq 2 \\sqrt{2}$<br />$\\Rightarrow t+\\frac{1}{t} \\geq 2 \\sqrt{2}$, where $2^x=t$<br />$\\Rightarrow t^2-2 \\sqrt{2} t+1 \\geq 0$<br />$\\Rightarrow x \\leq \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}-1)$<br />Also, $0 < \\sqrt{2}-1 < 1, \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}-1) < 0$.<br />$\\therefore$ The solution is<br />$\\left.\\left(-\\infty, \\log _2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\right)\\right] \\cup\\left[\\frac{1}{2}, \\infty\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
